WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.589
The mayor of Uvalde, Texas,

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.149
announced recently that Robb

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:04.379
Elementary School would be

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.399
demolished.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.079
"You can never ask a child to go

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.089
back or a teacher to go back in

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.129
that school ever",

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:11.939
he said.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.709
What happened in Uvalde was a

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.629
gruesome tragedy that exposes

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.159
some of American culture's worst

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.319
pathologies a fixation

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.209
on guns and violence,

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.189
untreated mental illness,

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.109
large swaths of alienated

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.569
and angry young men, incompetent

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.489
and unaccountable police.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.569
The media went looking for

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:31.769
solutions.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.209
What if we could keep guns out of

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:34.919
the wrong hands or get the right

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.149
people medicated?

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:37.469
Or reform the police?

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.479
Or fix what's plaguing angry

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.299
young men? All legitimate questions.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.239
But what the media rarely asks is,

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.279
are we part of the problem?

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.169
A growing body of research

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.549
says, yes.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.409
This is learned behavior.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.539
And the media coverage is is leading

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:56.609
more people to learn it and to

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:57.629
copy it.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:59.609
University of Alabama criminologist

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:01.319
Adam Lankford has studied mass

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.089
killers for more than a decade and

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.708
concluded, along with many other

00:01:04.709 --> 00:01:06.599
scholars, that the way the media

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.429
covers mass shootings

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:11.039
incentivizes more mass shootings,

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.959
and for the killers to create as

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.269
high a body count as possible.

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:18.519
He says fame seeking is a motivation

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.799
he's consistently observed across

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.659
the majority of mass shooters.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:24.519
The more victims they kill,

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:26.079
the more fame and attention they

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:27.939
get. We've seen that in the

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.409
United States, mass shootings have

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:31.599
become more deadly over time.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:33.399
And it seems to be directly related

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.749
to this.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.009
"There seems to be too much demand

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:37.539
for fame in America", Lankford

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:38.319
writes.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:39.609
And not enough supply.

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:41.469
We see people posting

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:43.659
videos and and outrageous

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:45.279
statements to get attention.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.259
Mass killings is just the most

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.329
extreme version of this, where

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.309
people aren't just being offensive

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:53.289
or outrageous to get attention.

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:54.309
And they know this works.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:56.409
Essentially, this is guaranteeing

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:58.569
them fame and celebrity

00:01:58.570 --> 00:01:59.229
status.

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:00.939
One of Lankford studies found that

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:02.769
winning a Super Bowl or Academy

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:04.659
Award garnered less media attention

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:06.249
than committing a high profile mass

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.049
killing. Perpetrators get pictured

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:09.369
more on front pages than their

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:10.839
individual victims.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.669
And there's a strong correlation

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:14.439
between the number of victims harmed

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.239
in these attacks and the amount of

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:17.829
media attention that perpetrators

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:18.669
receive.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:20.349
So the media is rewarding this.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:21.429
And, of course, you know, you can

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:22.989
think about, well, why did they do

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:23.990
that?

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.889
I think part of it is, is clickbait.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:28.779
Essentially, what was some of

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.479
the most striking evidence to you

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.789
that seeking this fame

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.009
and going out in a blaze of glory

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.859
was really a common motivation

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.779
for mass killers.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:42.699
The Columbine killers wanted to kill

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:43.929
250 people.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.339
That was their goal.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:46.479
And although they didn't kill as

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.219
many victims as they wanted, they

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:49.599
were talking about how movies would

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:50.829
be made about them.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.839
And they were talking about whether

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:54.159
Steven Spielberg or Quentin

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:55.929
Tarantino would be directing.

00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:57.609
Right. Certainly movies were made

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.349
about them and they've received a

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:00.879
tremendous amount of attention.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.769
And then we know from connecting

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:04.629
the dots that subsequent

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:05.919
shooters have considered the

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:07.809
Columbine killers to be role models.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:09.069
Of all the incidents that have

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:11.259
happened that inspired

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:13.149
copycats, Columbine seems to

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:15.009
be the one that stands out as

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:16.989
inspiring the most.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:18.279
You know, also, I guess if we just

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.379
think about the historical context,

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.239
you know, 24-seven cable

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:24.099
news was kind of

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.319
coming into the forefront

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:27.279
at that point. Right?

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:29.199
So there was a lot of desire

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.089
to fill time on

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:33.099
TV by covering current events.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.059
And this was a big one.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:35.739
Right. But, you know, some studies

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:37.899
suggest that like Columbine received

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:40.149
more attention than like major

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:41.440
U.S. military

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:44.529
events and incursions and

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:45.669
things like that. In other words,

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:48.369
that it received an outsized

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:50.439
amount of attention, given that,

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:52.059
as tragic as it was, you know, it

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:53.979
was relatively limited in terms

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.479
of the actual number of victims

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:56.259
killed.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:58.329
And yet, you know, it's its

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.159
actual influence has

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.409
been inflated and

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:04.479
and prompted by

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.639
the media coverage it received.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:08.679
Langford's 2019 study found

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.869
that at least 16 mass shooters

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:13.119
since Columbine have voiced fame

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:14.949
or notoriety as a motive,

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:16.689
and that the fame seekers tend to

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.369
have more than double the body

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:20.619
counts, and many articulated

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:22.449
a desire to surpass past

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:23.499
records.

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:25.899
Many of these mass shooters

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.639
don't particularly have any sort of

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:28.989
empathy for their victims, and

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:30.759
they're willing to kill their youth.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:32.769
They're using their victims as

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:34.539
the means to an end.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.629
And that end is fame

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.879
and what they would consider glory.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.709
In 2007, Virginia Tech was

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:43.509
the deadliest mass shooting in U.S.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.149
history. And then in 2016,

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:47.679
the Orlando Pulse nightclub shooting

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.149
was the deadliest mass shooting in

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:50.079
U.S. history.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:52.599
And then a year later, in 2017,

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.039
the Las Vegas mass shooting was the

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.239
deadliest mass shooting in U.S.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:56.079
history. Right.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.399
We see these kind of terrible

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.199
records being set and reset.

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:02.289
And since Columbine,

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:04.359
all eight of the most

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.429
lethal or deadliest mass shootings

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:08.139
have been committed by fame seekers.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:10.299
It's not just Langford saying this.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.339
A 2017 FBI report says

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:14.259
the dominance of 24-seven media

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:16.239
coverage perpetuates the mass

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:18.279
shooting phenomenon and allows

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:20.259
it to grow and evolve and

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:22.149
suggests news media should refrain

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:23.679
from naming the assailants, from

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.659
posting their photographs and videos

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.579
and communications, and

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:28.539
from publishing detailed

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:30.219
investigations into their lives and

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.349
motives. More than 100 researchers

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:34.239
have joined Langford in signing on

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:35.679
to the Don't Name Them Movement

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.779
petition, which asks major

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:39.489
media to adopt new norms for

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:41.079
covering mass killings.

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:43.029
Nobody looks in the face of

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:44.319
the most recent mass shooter and

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.239
thinks, Oh, now that I

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.159
see what he looks like,

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.259
I know how to stop these attacks

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:51.129
more effectively.

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:53.589
Sometimes you have a trial

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:55.119
of a mass shooter, you know, a year

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.189
later or sentencing period.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:59.229
And the pictures and

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:01.689
the names are continued to be used

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:03.309
in the coverage when it's no longer

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:04.239
news.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:06.729
And so I guess I just point to

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:08.379
kind of the thoughtless use of this

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:09.759
information as clickbait.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:11.619
I just want to be perfectly clear

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:13.659
that from my understanding of

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.059
this letter, that you and your.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.769
Colleagues have put out this call to

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:17.770
action.

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:20.519
You're not calling for any sort of

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.499
government intervention in terms of

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.389
limiting the right of the

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:25.619
media to publish certain

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:28.109
information. This is all norms

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:30.180
and voluntary action, correct?

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.759
Right. In other words, I guess we'd

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:35.069
like to encourage you or if it came

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:37.379
down to it, to shame these companies

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:39.419
into acting in a more

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.069
socially responsible way that

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:42.809
protects public health.

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:44.069
We're not saying the government

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.899
should formally

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:47.939
restrict this information.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:48.839
Again, I don't think that's

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.029
possible. It can lead to

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:52.829
even more mistrust of government.

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:54.869
Look, the people who work for

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:56.729
for media companies, they don't

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:58.739
want to see more people die.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:06:59.909
I think they just need to look a

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:02.279
little more closely at the evidence

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:04.379
and and take a look in the mirror

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:07.019
and say, can I make this problem

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:08.579
slightly less serious based on my

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:09.419
own actions?

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:11.039
There's a couple objections that

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:13.169
come to mind for me that I'd

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:15.359
be curious to hear your answer to.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.429
One is that when

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:19.319
I think of the idea of media

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:21.479
curtailing coverage in certain ways,

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:23.969
like not showing people's faces

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:26.099
or their names or going into

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.199
their motivations and manifestos,

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:30.269
one is that the information

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:32.129
will get out there on less

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.029
reputable sites.

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:34.829
We're in the digital age now, so,

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:36.689
you know, now more than ever, the

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:37.799
information is going to get out

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:39.959
there. You're generating maybe

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:41.369
something approximating a black

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:43.109
market in information.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:45.599
And that's where disinformation

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:47.639
thrives and perhaps even creates

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:49.709
even more of a taboo,

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:51.419
maybe in some deranged way, even

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:53.729
more a more romantic aura around

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:55.079
these guys.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:56.639
How can we avoid that?

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.499
So I think it's a it's a good point.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:00.689
In other words, like, I'm under no

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:03.029
kind of delusion

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:04.949
that this information won't

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.059
get out in some ways.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.679
I guess what I would just say is the

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:09.719
degree of attention

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:11.129
matters. In other words, it's not

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:12.809
binary. It's not either that

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:15.029
information is completely

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:17.039
kept silent or it's totally

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:18.869
out there. Less coverage is

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:20.249
meaningful, right?

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:21.389
We're not going to cut out all

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:22.169
coverage.

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:24.059
But if we don't give these mass

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:25.979
shooters, Super Bowl type like

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.869
advertising for

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:29.879
the terrible things they do

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:31.199
and just kind of have it more

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.459
restrained.

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:34.408
That in itself would would make

00:08:34.409 --> 00:08:35.099
a difference.

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:37.259
Suppressing any kind of information

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:39.569
could lead us to missing some

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:41.939
kind of important pattern or clue

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:43.769
that could prevent the next one

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:44.849
of these from happening.

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:46.889
Like what if there was a series

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:48.899
of connected ideological

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:50.729
killings that we don't fully

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:52.379
understand because there's kind of

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.899
like a media blackout

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:57.179
on covering

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:59.009
the full extent of what's going

00:08:59.010 --> 00:08:59.939
on here.

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:01.829
Don't limit any information

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:04.019
about warning signs or backgrounds.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.209
That's all very important

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:07.649
and needs to be discussed and needs

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.869
to be analyzed carefully.

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:11.849
Just, you know, keep in mind

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:14.999
that the face itself is not useful.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.439
And there are other ways to refer to

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:18.419
someone and

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:19.409
have everybody know who you're

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:20.849
talking about based on the date of

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:22.469
the event and the location of the

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:24.239
event, without really giving that

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:26.189
person's name the

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:29.009
attention that he craved

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:30.869
as part of his decision to attack.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.179
Is there a sense that this is really

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:35.009
something that is going

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:37.079
to take years, maybe

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:38.909
decades, to see some

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:40.620
sort of effect reversing?

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.429
Well, I guess it just depends on how

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:46.259
dramatic the change or

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:47.379
the intervention is.

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:49.349
Right. So if

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:51.389
major media organizations

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:53.579
change their processes in subtle

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.589
ways and don't tell anyone about

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:57.509
it, then I don't expect

00:09:57.510 --> 00:09:59.609
mass shooters to to change

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:00.569
what they're doing at all.

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:02.429
Right. The best thing would be

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:04.319
if major media companies came out

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:05.969
and said, we're no longer going to

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:07.799
publish the names or faces

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:08.849
of mass shooters.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:10.079
And then the next time a mass

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.909
shooting happens, which it will,

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:12.869
they stuck to that.

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:14.399
Right. That would send a powerful

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:15.600
message. And

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:18.629
and the mass shooters, I think,

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:20.579
would start to learn that they can't

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:22.259
be rewarded in the way they were in

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:22.829
the past.

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:24.719
Just searching some of

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:26.579
the recent killers names

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:28.229
on some of the major media sites

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:30.329
will show you that these measures

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:32.789
are far from being the norm today.

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:34.979
But have you seen any signs

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:37.289
of progress or reason to hope

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:39.269
for improvement in the recent

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:40.169
in recent years?

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:42.719
Or are you pessimistic

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:44.579
about any near-term change?

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.529
It's a great question.

00:10:46.530 --> 00:10:47.609
One of the things I've seen, which

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:49.469
was a little disturbing is

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:50.759
some members of the media kind of

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:52.499
patting themselves on the back as if

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:53.279
mission accomplished.

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:55.019
We've already changed how the media

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:57.019
covers mass shootings and

00:10:57.020 --> 00:10:58.919
and I don't think that's the case.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.449
One thing that has been a change is

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:01.889
I think you've seen more attention

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:03.239
given to the victims of mass

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:05.429
shootings, but

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:06.899
that doesn't fix the problem.

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:08.189
In other words, like doing something

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:10.049
good on the one hand doesn't

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:11.549
mean that the other things you're

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:13.319
doing that are dangerous or any less

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:14.159
dangerous.

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:15.539
There are more media companies than

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:16.769
ever before, and there's kind of

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:18.839
more competition for media companies

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:19.869
for eyeballs.

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:20.729
Right. It's not like we just have

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:22.619
three news stations and a

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:24.179
couple of major newspapers or things

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:24.959
like that.

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:27.209
And unfortunately, like the pressure

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:29.159
felt by members of the media

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:30.569
because of the competition that

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:32.549
they're involved in, sometimes seems

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:34.499
to be leading them to

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.389
resist change, even if there's lots

00:11:36.390 --> 00:11:37.649
of evidence suggesting it would be

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:39.299
the right thing to do.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:40.739
Many of us know the names of the

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:42.569
Columbine shooters and the

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:44.699
names of many other killers.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:46.139
How many victims names do you

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:47.279
remember?

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:48.959
Or how about this name?

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:49.960
Elijah Deacon.

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:52.979
Do you know Elijah Deacon?

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:54.209
I'm about to show you some of his

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:56.219
work, and I want to give you fair

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:57.179
warning.

00:11:57.180 --> 00:11:59.369
Skip ahead about 15 seconds

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:01.079
if you don't want to see something

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:03.259
quite gory and disturbing.

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:04.260
Okay, ready?

00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:08.339
That's what's left of a murderer

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:10.139
whom Dicken gunned down in a

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:12.269
shopping mall after he'd killed

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:13.979
three innocents.

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:15.779
Many more people would have died if

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:17.279
Dickens hadn't intervened, said the

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:18.569
local police chief.

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:20.549
If more angry young men thinking

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:22.319
about doing something horrible saw

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:24.149
pictures like that instead of mug

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:26.669
shots or old school photos,

00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:28.409
would they maybe think twice before

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:30.059
going on shooting sprees?

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.559
Demolishing the school building

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:33.449
where this tragedy occurred won't

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:34.529
do anything to stop it from

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:35.909
happening again.

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:37.799
But burying the legacies of the men

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:40.169
responsible for such atrocities

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:41.170
just might help.

